From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] sleh: emulate LSE atomics in kernel mode too

libfirehose_kernel and the other prebuilt Apple libraries linked into the
kernel (see kernel.development.sagit.linkarguments) are compiled with LSE
enabled, so -march=armv8-a on our own translation units cannot help there.
The kernel boot died inside __firehose_buffer_tracepoint_reserve with

  Undefined kernel instruction: pc=... instr=c8b37f08   (cas x19, x8, [x24])

Gate sagit_handle_lse() on the instruction encoding only instead of on
PSR64_IS_USER64, so EL1 faults get the same LDXR/STXR emulation.
---
 osfmk/arm64/sleh.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c b/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
@@ -1347,11 +1347,13 @@
 #if defined(SAGIT)
 	/*
 	 * SAGIT has no LSE atomics (ARMv8.0). Emulate userspace LSE
 	 * instructions by trapping them here.
 	 */
-	if (PSR64_IS_USER64(get_saved_state_cpsr(state))) {
-		if (sagit_handle_lse(state, instr)) {
-			return;
-		}
-	}
+	/*
+	 * Prebuilt Apple libraries (libfirehose_kernel, libcc_kext) are built
+	 * with LSE, so kernel-mode code needs the same emulation as userspace.
+	 */
+	if (sagit_handle_lse(state, instr)) {
+		return;
+	}
 #endif
 
 #if CONFIG_DTRACE
